{
  "date": "2026-11-12",
  "category": "finance",
  "title_zh": "央行报告比较十年利率：中国房贷利率降到3.1%",
  "title_en": "PBOC report compares ten years of interest rates: China's mortgage rate falls to 3.1%",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "zh": "11月11日，中国人民银行发布了今年第三季度的货币政策执行报告。这份报告里有一个专门的部分，把中国过去十年的利率和美国、欧元区、日本等发达经济体做了比较。",
      "en": "On November 11, the People's Bank of China released its Monetary Policy Report for the third quarter of this year. The report has a special section that compares China's interest rates over the past ten years with those of developed economies such as the United States, the euro area and Japan."
    },
    {
      "zh": "报告说，9月新发放的企业贷款利率不到3%，新的个人住房贷款利率大约是3.1%。在过去十年里，中国的房贷利率最高是5.8%，现在降到了这十年最低的水平。相比之下，美国现在的房贷利率是5.3%，日本是4.4%，欧元区是3.6%。",
      "en": "The report says that the interest rate on new corporate loans issued in September was below 3%, and the rate on new personal housing loans was about 3.1%. Over the past ten years, China's highest mortgage rate was 5.8%, and it has now fallen to the lowest level of the decade. By comparison, the current mortgage rate is 5.3% in the US, 4.4% in Japan and 3.6% in the euro area."
    },
    {
      "zh": "报告还比较了公司债券和国债之间的利差。中国的这个利差大约是30个基点。报告提到，在政策利率接近零的时候，美国、日本和欧元区的这个利差分别大约是120、80和50个基点。一个基点等于0.01个百分点。",
      "en": "The report also compared the spread between corporate bonds and government bonds. In China this spread is about 30 basis points. The report mentions that when policy rates were close to zero, this spread was about 120, 80 and 50 basis points in the US, Japan and the euro area respectively. One basis point equals 0.01 percentage points."
    },
    {
      "zh": "央行表示，存款利率降低以后，贷款利率才有下降的空间，因为银行需要保持一定的利差，才能稳定经营。另外，央行还提醒，在中国，国债的利息收入不用交所得税，所以比较不同国家的利率时，也要考虑税的影响。",
      "en": "The central bank said that only after deposit rates come down is there room for loan rates to fall, because banks need to keep a certain spread in order to operate steadily. In addition, the central bank pointed out that in China, interest income from government bonds is not subject to income tax, so the effect of taxes should also be considered when comparing interest rates across countries."
    }
  ],
